{"candidates":[{"content":"Adopt a proof-theoretic grounding: define acceptance by existence of a canonical, polynomial-time-checkable dialectical proof tree whose leaves are committed roots, and treat the fixed-point labeling only as a sanity check. This changes the semantics from a global fixed point to a local proof search. Criticizable because proof-tree existence may not be monotone under edge addition unless the tree language is carefully restricted, and it may reintroduce self-support if cycles are not handled explicitly.","typicality":0.3,"neighbours":["SRC_003","SRC_007"]},{"content":"Strengthen the grounded extension by adding an explicit defeat-priority total order over attacks, computed by a canonical polynomial-time rule. A node is accepted if it is defended against all higher-priority attackers, and reinstatement becomes a consequence of priority order rather than an emergent property. Criticizable because any priority order introduces arbitrary tie-breaking that may not reflect evidence strength, and the rule may be manipulable by synthetic edge ordering.","typicality":0.45,"neighbours":["SRC_002","SRC_004"]},{"content":"Use a semiring of evidence, e.g., tropical or fuzzy, to assign each attack a weight and each defense a contribution; acceptance is determined by solving a polynomial-time system of equations over the semiring, with the grounded extension as the least solution. This generalizes integer weights but changes the algebraic structure. Criticizable because the choice of semiring is not uniquely justified and may make reinstatement non-structural or require an additional fixpoint that breaks polynomial cost.","typicality":0.35,"neighbours":["SRC_004","SRC_008"]},{"content":"Prove an impossibility boundary: any monotone edge-construction enrichment that preserves determinism, polynomial cost, and committed-root validity cannot increase the set of accepted conjectures beyond the original grounded extension; therefore the only responsible strengthening is to enrich the vocabulary of defeat, e.g., typed attacks with side conditions, rather than the graph. Criticizable because the proof may rely on a too-restrictive definition of edge-construction and miss enrichment via annotations or proof certificates.","typicality":0.2,"neighbours":["SRC_002","SRC_007"]},{"content":"Make the grounded extension robust to future evidence by computing, in polynomial time, a suspension region of nodes whose status would change under any single edge addition; these nodes are labelled SUSPENDED-REVISABLE and the fixed point is augmented with this region as a derived annotation. Criticizable because sensitivity analysis may require examining all possible edge additions and could become exponential unless restricted to local perturbations, and the annotation may not be stable across graph revisions.","typicality":0.5,"neighbours":["SRC_005","SRC_006"]},{"content":"Introduce a commitment-root validity oracle: require every accepted node to have a shortest defense path to a committed root, and strengthen acceptance by requiring the path to be witness-minimal under a polynomial-time canonical ordering. This gives a graded notion of commitment and makes reinstatement a property of path-minimality. Criticizable because shortest paths may not capture argumentative reinstatement, and the canonical ordering may be manipulable by adding redundant defense paths.","typicality":0.4,"neighbours":["SRC_001","SRC_003"]}]}